    "topicLabel": "General English · written",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "Read the following passage carefully and answer the question that follows. Exercise is essential for maintaining a healthy lifestyle. It helps improve cardiovascular health, strengthens muscles, and boosts the immune system. Regular physical activity also reduces the risk of chronic diseases such as heart disease, diabetes, and obesity. Additionally, exercise plays a crucial role in mental well-being by reducing stress, anxiety, and depression. There are different types of exercises, including aerobic exercises like running and swimming, strength training like weightlifting, and flexibility exercises such as yoga and stretching. A combination of these exercises ensures overall fitness and health. Experts recommend at least 30 minutes of moderate exercise per day to maintain good health. The lack of physical activity has become a major concern, especially with modern lifestyles that involve sitting for long hours. Many people spend excessive time on screens, leading to a sedentary lifestyle. This can result in weight gain, muscle weakness, and poor cardiovascular health. To stay active, individuals can take small steps such as walking instead of driving, using stairs instead of elevators, and participating in sports or outdoor activities. Governments and health organizations promote exercise through awareness campaigns, fitness programs, and policies that encourage active lifestyles. Schools also play a key role by including physical education in their curriculum. Exercise is not just about fitness—it is a way to enhance the quality of life and increase life expectancy. Questions:\na. __________________ exercise includes activities like running and swimming(1)\nb. A sedentary lifestyle can lead to __________________ gain(1)\nc. Synonym of ‘guarantee’ (second paragraph)(1)\nd. Antonym of ‘diminish’ (fourth paragraph)(1)",
