    "question": "What did Grandfather Hari say about the small green shoot beside the cherry tree?",
    "explanation": "Model answer (2 marks, two or three sentences): Grandfather Hari pointed to the small green shoot growing beside the cherry tree and said proudly that the little plant had been only a seed when Binya's father was a boy. He told her to look at how much it had grown, and said that someday it would give shade to travellers long after he and Binya were gone. The two marks are carried by the two facts - that it was a mere seed in her father's boyhood, and that it will one day shade travellers after they are gone - so a candidate who mentions only the growth and omits the future shade should expect one mark. Write it in your own words and in reported speech; do not simply copy the quoted lines.",
    "guidance": "Model answer (2 marks, two or three sentences): Grandfather Hari pointed to the small green shoot growing beside the cherry tree and said proudly that the little plant had been only a seed when Binya's father was a boy. He told her to look at how much it had grown, and said that someday it would give shade to travellers long after he and Binya were gone. The two marks are carried by the two facts - that it was a mere seed in her father's boyhood, and that it will one day shade travellers after they are gone - so a candidate who mentions only the growth and omits the future shade should expect one mark. Write it in your own words and in reported speech; do not simply copy the quoted lines.",
