    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "Write an essay choosing one of the topics given below:\n(a) The role of NGOs in community development.\n(b) Minimum Government, Maximum Governance\n(c) Challenges faced by working women in modern society.",
    "explanation": "Ten marks for one essay means roughly 400-500 words in four to five paragraphs: an introduction that states your position, two or three body paragraphs each carrying one argument plus one concrete example, and a conclusion that resolves rather than repeats. Pick the topic you can supply specifics for, and prefer Mizoram/North-East examples since the examiner is an MPSC board. For (a), build around what NGOs do that government cannot — last-mile reach, community mobilisation, pilot innovation — with Mizoram examples (church-based welfare bodies, YMA, Mizo Hmeichhe Insuihkhawm Pawl) and be honest about limits: dependence on donor funding, weak accountability, patchy coverage. For (b), define the slogan (fewer intrusive processes, more effective delivery), then evidence it — self-attestation, DBT, single-window clearances, decriminalising minor offences, GST — and note the tension that 'minimum government' must not mean a withdrawn state in welfare or regulation. For (c), organise the challenges into the wage/promotion gap, the double burden of unpaid domestic work, workplace safety and harassment (POSH Act, 2013), child-care and maternity provision, and social attitudes; close with remedies (creches, flexible hours, transparent promotion criteria, paternity leave) rather than only lament. Do not pad with proverbs or quotations; examiners mark structure, specificity and clean grammar.",
