    "explanation": "In the standard four-phase account of India's population growth, 1951-1981 is the period of population explosion: death rates fell sharply with better health care and food security while birth rates stayed high, pushing annual growth above 2 per cent. 1901-1921 is the stagnant phase (1921 being the 'demographic divide'), 1921-1951 steady growth, and 1981 onwards high but decelerating growth.",
